  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_durnar",
      "name": {
        "en": "Dur-nar's Badge",
        "zh": "坚雷证章",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_durnar",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Dur-nar has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for preservation of the front while inflicting Arts casualties on the enemy.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Defender Operator during field operations to exercise Arts Protector responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员坚雷擅长在维持战线的同时对敌人造成法术杀伤\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为重装干员，行使驭法铁卫职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_durnar",
      "name": {
        "en": "A Guardian's Path",
        "zh": "守护的道路",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "X",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_durnar",
      "description": {
        "en": "'Didn't think we'd be starting with this wooden shield... Alright, this one's my oldest friend, which might surprise people who think it's just a chopping board, haha. But it's the gear I got back in boot camp.\n'I still remember my old drill instructor. He was really fierce, not like other Columbians. He always chewed me out for going 'offense offense offense' when trying to break through enemy lines. He told me there's no shortage of killers on the front lines of battle. Probably the least surprising type to run into.\n'But what's really worth counting on in the chaos is the sort of person who can get everyone else feeling like they'd live a few days longer with that person in front.\n'At the time, I never would've thought the first real combat in my life was just around the corner. It was a feint attack, but thanks to the enemy artillery, we suffered heavier losses than expected.\n'This shield... I actually picked it up from a fallen comrade. Out of the entire rearguard, I was the only one left... You can tell how desperate the fighting was by how damaged it is.\n'After the war, I got given a commendation in the form of THIS shield with Columbia's coat of arms etched on it. Its materials and make are a lot better than the ones we had during the war. Shame it never got to see combat.\n'You know what happened next. It was my first time being an instructor. I might have mocked Hank and the rest all the time, saying if they couldn't even get past me, they'd just be cannon fodder the moment they put boots on the ground. But in my heart, I knew they were the finest of soldiers, my very first point of pride. So when I got the order to send them on a suicide mission, I wanted nothing more than to use this shield to beat the shit out of the old bastard who gave the order.\n'Then we get to today... Here, on my Rhodes Island-retrofitted one. This scratch is from Fang, this dent is from Beagle, these arrow marks are thanks to Kroos... And now look at you all—more mature, taller, and even better in battle to boot. Really warms my heart, y'know... Feels like a good time to reminisce.\n'...*sigh* Honestly, what I'm doing now isn't too different from what I used to do. Just letting them know about all the hard knocks I've lived through, in my own way. But this doesn't mean they're taking a shortcut, because there's plenty of setbacks waiting for them out there, and how they handle them is something no one else can teach.\n'All I can do is stress again and again that killing is never the goal. It's only to be used to protect more people. Victory can only be enjoyed by the living, after all.\n'Alright, that's everything for my report. Oh, right, those retrofit plans I submitted earlier, still not approved? 'Impractical'? What do you mean, 'impractical'?! All I'm asking for is a little snack-holder on the inside so I can show my appreciation to the kids after training! It's how I teach, c'mon, be a little flexible, please, I'm begging you!'\n—From a recording of Dur-nar's promotion report",
        "zh": "“竟然要从这面木盾开始……好吧，它是我最久的老朋友了，甚至还被路过的同事当成过菜板哈哈。但这是我刚在军队受训时的装备。\n“我还记得那位负责训练我的教官，不像其他哥伦比亚人，他很严苛，总是批评我只会用进攻打开局面。他告诉我，战场上会杀人的前卫太多了，杀人是战场最不足为奇的事。\n“在战场上真正值得托付的，是往前面一站，别人就知道，自己又能多活几天的那种人。\n“谁想到，没过多久我人生的第一次实战就来了。那是一场佯攻，在敌人恐怖的炮火下，我们遭受的损失还是远远超出了预期。\n“所以这面盾牌……其实是我从倒下的战友手里捡起来的。那批垫后的人里只剩我一个了……你们从它的毁损程度也看得出有多惨烈了。\n“那一战之后，军队以表彰为名头，把那面印有哥伦比亚国徽的盾颁给了我。它的做工和材质比我们前卫队在战场上配备的都好。可惜它并没有出现在战场上。\n“再后来你们也清楚啦，那也是我第一次当教官。虽然我总嘲笑汉克他们，要是连我都越不过去，去了战场也是凑数的……可在我心里，他们就是最好的兵，他们是我最开始的骄傲。所以当后面我接到要他们去当敢死队的指令，我想都没想就把这盾砸在了那个死老头脸上。\n“最后就是现在啦……看，在罗德岛特别改装的这面上，这个擦痕是芬的，这个凹陷是米格鲁的，这几道箭痕是克洛丝的……而如今的大家也成长为了更成熟的模样，个头蹿高了，战斗的表现也更精湛了，真是欣慰呀……欣慰到甚至有些怀念呢。\n“……嗐，其实我现在做的事儿，和以前也没多大区别。只是把所有吃过的亏磕过的坎，都用我自己的方式告诉他们而已。但这绝不意味着走捷径。因为，肯定还有不计其数的新挫折等待着他们。而如何面对那些挫折，是旁人无论如何都没办法教的。\n“我只能反复向他们强调，杀敌人永远不是目的，杀敌人是为了保护更多人——战场的胜利永远只属于活着的人。\n“好啦，要述职的内容就是这些。哦，对了，前段时间我提交的那个改造方案还没通过吗？不实用？哪里不实用了？！就是在盾后面多加个放零食的空间，这样训练完以后，我好慰劳那些小家伙们不是吗？！这是我的教学习惯啦，通融通融，拜托了！”\n——来自坚雷的晋升述职录音",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
